      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A national historic landmark in Napoleonville is the Madewood Plantation, a former sugar cane plantation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleonville%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Assumption Parish Courthouse, built in 1896, remains a functioning government building and a key historic landmark in Napoleonville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleonville%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Napoleonville sits on the eastern bank of Bayou Lafourche, a 106‑mile distributary of the Mississippi that once powered regional transport and farming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleonville%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The village is best known as the location where the film Because of Winn‑Dixie, based on Kate DiCamillo's Newbery Prize‑winning novel, was shot.",
